    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` with a 400 response, following the existing Spring conventions in the codebase (dedicated business-rule exception + `@ControllerAdvice` handler).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New exception** `rest/advice/FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeException` pattern.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `FutureRegistrationDateException` to `400 Bad Request`, reporting the `registrationDate` field (consistent with the other field-level validation handlers).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `resolveRegistrationDate`, the *supplied* date (before the business-day roll-forward) is now checked against `LocalDate.now()`; if it's later, the new exception is thrown. A `null` (unsupplied) date still defaults to the server date, and the weekend roll-forward is unchanged.\n\nThe target test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate` of `2999-01-01`) now returns 400, and the full suite is green.",
